 status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1174903A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>JAPAN SCIENCE &amp; TECH CORP</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>YAMAGUCHI KENTARO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YAMAGUCHI, KENTARO</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>YAMAGUCHI KENTARO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YAMAGUCHI, KENTARO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for electrospray ionization mass spectrometric analysis which comprises cooling a sample to be analyzed which contains a solvent and flows out from a spray fine tube with an inert gas for low temperature vaporization (A), and carrying out ionization and a mass spectrometric analysis of the sample while cooling a chamber (7) for removing a solvent or an ion source block (8) with liquid nitrogen; and an apparatus for the method.  The method can be used for analyzing exactly a mass of a molecular ion or a fragment ion of an unstable organometallic complex or a polymeric organic compound.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé d'analyse spectrométrique ES-MS, qui consiste à refroidir un échantillon à analyser, contenant un solvant et s'écoulant d'un tube de pulvérisation fine, à l'aide d'un gaz inerte pour la vaporisation (A) à faible température, à ioniser et à assurer une analyse spectrométrique de masse de l'échantillon alors qu'une chambre (7) est refroidie, de sorte qu'un solvant ou un bloc source d'ions (8) soit enlevé à l'aide d'azote liquide. L'invention porte également sur un appareil pour la mise en oeuvre du procédé. Le procédé de l'invention peut être utilisé pour l'analyse exacte de la masse d'un ion moléculaire ou d'un ion fragment d'un complexe organométallique instable ou d'un composé organique polymère.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>